  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": 13973,
      "content": "On Tuesday, October 13 at 6:33 a.m. ET, Falcon 9 launched Dragon\u2019s 35th Commercial Resupply Services (CRS-35) mission to the International Space Station from Space Launch Complex 40 (SLC-40) at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida. After an approximate 52-hour flight, Dragon autonomously docked with the orbiting laboratory on Thursday, October 15 at 10:27 a.m. ET."
    },
    {
      "id": 13974,
      "content": "CRS-35 is the fourth flight for the Dragon spacecraft supporting this mission, which previously flew CRS-26, CRS-29, and CRS-33 to and from the space station."
    },
    {
      "id": 13975,
      "content": "This was the eighth flight of the first stage booster supporting this mission, which previously launched KF-01, IMAP, NROL-77, GPS III-9, CRS-34, NROL-95, and one Starlink mission. Following stage separation, the first stage landed on Landing Zone 40 at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida."
    }
  ]
